    "notes": "The decision to run was actually at around 11:42. There is a description of the game up to that point below. \n\nFrom ohno's perspective, the game opens with a 3v4 in the backdoor. ohno's warrior collapses through mid to make it a 4v4 and they manage to push xxx back to their footies briefly. The fight turns and ohno retreats to their backdoor footies. ohno's mesmer collapses through mid to make it a 5v4. xxx retreats to backdoor footies and their prot arrives through pit to make it a 5v5. ohno's mesmer returns to mainteam through mid whilst xxx's prot returns to mainteam through pit/frontdoor. \n\n4v4 is relatively even, though ohno seems to get pushed back. At 6:50, ohno's derv joins split through pit/backdoor but xxx's prot matches on time through mid for 5v5 again. Around 7:40, ohno switches the composition of the 4v4 split and sends mesmer over air ele, where air ele now takes over flag duty. He initiates a double run with the derv of ohno, waiting back for second flag at 7:55. At 8:27, he drops the flag to the derv (both players are halfrunning) and goes to pick up another flag. Air ele then full runs the flag while mainteam pushes towards enemy footies. xxx's mesmer collapses split through mid so ohno has a powerplay at main with the flag capped. Enemy derv starts to run flag at 10:03. Air ele responds almost instantly and goes back to run flag whilst mainteam pushes the pit 3v4 then 3v3. Enemy caps at 10:39 and our air ele overcaps at 10:59. mainteam is stuck in a 3v4 in their pit once running enemy derv returns to base. Air ele follows now that flag is capped towards mainteam and takes outside archer. \n\nEnemy mesmer takes flag up a bit to drop it to enemy derev, who starts running at 11:21. Air ele waits for 20s pushing the flag and then goes back to run a flag. Air ele caps at 12:54."
